<title>FINLAND: KESKO SAYS EU ACCEPTS ANDERSEN AS TRUSTEE.</title>
<headline>KESKO SAYS EU ACCEPTS ANDERSEN AS TRUSTEE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish wholesaler and retailer Kesko said in a statement on Tuesday the European Commission had approved auditing and consulting firm Arthur Andersen as an independent trustee to monitor the sale of Tuko.</p>
<p>Kesko proposed Arthur Andersen after the commission required a trustee to make sure the buyer of Tuko would &quot;possess the necessary skills and resources to ensure that the divested business constitutes an active and competitive force&quot;.</p>
<p>Kesko bought its rival Tuko in May last year but was ordered by the commission to sell it to restore competition on the daily goods market in Finland.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
